sec.p:
Three prespecified sensitivity analyses were performed:
(1) replacement of the random-effects model with a fixed-effect model;
(2) restriction to studies at low risk of bias after exclusion of studies rated as some concerns or high risk of bias;
(3) leave-one-out analysis, in which each study was sequentially omitted to examine the influence of individual trials on the pooled estimate and on the direction and statistical significance of the overall result.
